sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-dasypus-novemcinctus-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dasypus-novemcinctus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dasypus-novemcinctus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 4.108 µm on Holocene Dasypus novemcinctus dermis (Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 86.8/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 overall 86.8/100, superseding the Pass 1 audit at 77.2. The diffusion-scale sweep tracks the analytic wavelength with Pearson r = 0.999999 and RMSE = 0.524 µm. Equal diffusivities collapse the activator. The specimen mask is non-circular (circularity 0.144 versus 1) and the dorsal Sobel counter returns 12 peaks versus the nominal nine bands. Chronoseries length is 1 at 0 Ma; 66 detail wavelengths fit in the 273 µm primordium interval. No second assessor. Overall 86.8/100 (faithfulness 85.6, reproducibility 89.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/dasypus_novemcinctus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-dasypus-novemcinctus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 1008876 B, 1248×984 px, artifact_sha256 aeacb08e61f21379327f275c4ac1a48723842b659db91269b46983bf4e02b2a6 (sha256 aeacb08e61f21379327f275c4ac1a48723842b659db91269b46983bf4e02b2a6), spec_fingerprint 0ed1ba81083be6f146345ad2f0ef47d7ab333edbbcd8e4d2c467f1b152acb7c7. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 0ed1ba81083be6f146345ad2f0ef47d7ab333edbbcd8e4d2c467f1b152acb7c7; artifact_sha256: aeacb08e61f21379327f275c4ac1a48723842b659db91269b46983bf4e02b2a6; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/dasypus_novemcinctus_turing_wavelength_s0/dasypus_novemcinctus_specimen.jpg=7f1ba0e3ab8bdb13..., datasets/dasypus_novemcinctus_turing_wavelength_s0/dasypus_novemcinctus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=e8ce5113e12fa07c...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-dasypus-novemcinctus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Vickaryous and Hall (2006) describe the banded shield and hexagonal osteoderm rosettes of Dasypus novemcinctus. | Turing (1952) gives k_c from the dispersion relation; Schnakenberg (1979) gives the two-species kinetics.; reconstructed_in_script: a=0.10, b=0.90, D_v/D_u=20, D_u solved so linear λ_c=4.108 µm. Sweep scales both diffusivities by 0.64 to 1.69. | Pearson r=0.999999 between measured and analytic wavelengths, RMSE=0.524 µm, replicate CV=0.029, ablation amplitude ratio about 5.1e4. | Photograph segmentation: foreground fraction 0.350, circularity 0.144, coherency 0.411, Sobel band count 12 against the nominal 9, shoulder spacing 72 px.; transfer_boundary: 4.108 µm is the assigned detail rung at 0 Ma, not a length reported by Chen or Vickaryous. The photograph is the whole animal. | The GIF reuses the photograph's mid-frequency edges so the computer-vision comparison is not an independent drawing.; does_not_claim: That osteoderm rosettes are generated by a 4.1 µm Turing instability. | That the Sobel peak count of 12 is a manual census of the nine movable bands. | That RMSE of 0.52 µm has been removed; the correlation is high because the error is a nearly constant factor of 1.12.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Independent second assessor. Both passes are single-assessor (Grok 4.7).', 'status': 'open'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R7', 'item': 'Dorsal Sobel band count is 12 against the nominal nine movable bands. The counter is not a manual shield census.', 'status': 'open'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R8', 'item': 'Saturated wavelength remains about 1.12 times the linear 4.108 µm (RMSE 0.524 µm) even though the sweep correlation is above 0.98.', 'status': 'open'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R9', 'item': 'No 4.1 µm histological micrograph of Dasypus dermis is in the dataset. The specimen is an organism-scale photograph.', 'status': 'open'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.868"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (single builder-assessor; second provider still open as R5)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

